# Customer quality templates (TECH 4).

block customer_header
section cust_id | Customer and product | 3
f cq_customer | Customer | customer | *
f cq_customer_ref | Customer reference | text
f cq_contact | Customer contact | text
f cq_part | Part | part
f cq_product | Product | product
f cq_lot | Lot, serial or date code | text
f cq_received | Received on | date | *
f cq_owner | Owner | user | *
end

block customer_signatures
sign cq_prepared | Prepared by | prepared | I prepared this record and the information in it is complete.
sign cq_reviewed | Reviewed by | reviewed | I reviewed this record. | complaints.edit
sign cq_approved | Approved by | approved | I approve this record. | complaints.approve
end

template complaint-intake | Complaint Intake | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags complaint, intake, customer feedback
purpose Capture a customer complaint completely at first contact: who, what, where, when, how many, the evidence and what the customer expects, and decide how it is handled.
scope Every complaint about product, service or delivery, received by any channel.
instructions Record the customer's words. Ask for samples, photos and lot information. Assess safety and reportability at intake; urgent complaints are escalated the same day.
workflow Received, triaged, assigned, acknowledged to the customer.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use customer_header
section intake | Complaint | 2
f ci_channel | Received by | choice | * [E-mail; Phone; Portal; Sales; Field service; Social media; Regulator]
f ci_description | Complaint in the customer's words | longtext | *
f ci_category | Category | choice | * [Product quality; Function or performance; Delivery; Packaging or labelling; Documentation; Service; Safety]
f ci_qty | Quantity affected | integer | min=0
f ci_expectation | What the customer expects | longtext
f ci_samples | Samples to be returned | boolean
f ci_evidence | Photos and evidence | attachment
section triage | Triage | 3
f ci_safety | Safety concern | boolean | *
f ci_reportable | Possibly reportable to a regulator | boolean | *
f ci_severity | Severity | choice | * [Critical; Major; Minor]
f ci_priority | Priority | calc | {IF(OR(ci_safety, ci_reportable, ci_severity = "Critical"), "Urgent", IF(ci_severity = "Major", "High", "Normal"))}
f ci_ack_due | Acknowledge by | date
f ci_route | Handled as | choice | [Complaint investigation; Return; Warranty; Information only]
rule ci_priority | equals | Urgent | #FDE7E9 | bold
rule ci_priority | equals | High | #FFF4D6 | bold
use customer_signatures
end

template return-authorization | Return Authorization | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags RMA, return, authorization
purpose Authorize the return of product from a customer: the reason, the quantity, the shipping instructions and how the returned product will be handled.
scope Returns for evaluation, credit, repair or replacement.
instructions Give the customer the authorization number and the shipping instructions. Returned product is received into quarantine until evaluated.
workflow Requested, authorized, shipped by customer, received, evaluated, closed.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
use customer_header
section rma | Return | 2
f rma_number | Return authorization number | text
f rma_reason | Reason | choice | * [Defective; Wrong part; Damaged in transit; Excess stock; Warranty; Evaluation requested]
f rma_complaint | Related complaint | record
f rma_qty | Quantity authorized | integer | * min=1
f rma_qty_received | Quantity received | integer | min=0
f rma_instructions | Shipping instructions | longtext
f rma_disposition | Planned handling | choice | [Evaluate; Credit; Replace; Repair and return; Scrap at customer]
f rma_expires | Authorization valid until | date
f rma_qty_check | Received matches authorized | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(rma_qty_received), IF(rma_qty_received = rma_qty, "Yes", "No"), "")}
rule rma_qty_check | equals | No | #FFF4D6 | bold
use customer_signatures
end

template returned-product-evaluation | Returned Product Evaluation | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags returned product, failure analysis, evaluation
purpose Evaluate returned product to confirm or not the reported failure, find the failure mode and decide the outcome for each unit.
scope Product returned for evaluation.
instructions Record the condition as received before testing. Test each unit. A failure that cannot be reproduced is recorded as no fault found, with the tests done.
workflow Received, evaluated, outcome decided, results shared with the customer.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use customer_header
section rpe_receipt | Receipt | 2
f rpe_rma | Return authorization | record
f rpe_condition | Condition as received | longtext | *
f rpe_photos | Photos as received | photo
section rpe_units | Units evaluated | 1
table rpe_rows | Units | 1
c ru_serial | Serial or identification | text | *
c ru_reported | Reported failure | text
c ru_tests | Tests performed | text | *
c ru_confirmed | Failure confirmed | choice | * [Confirmed; Not confirmed - no fault found; Different failure found]
c ru_mode | Failure mode | text
c ru_cause | Cause category | choice | [Design; Manufacturing; Supplier; Handling; Misuse; Wear; Unknown]
c ru_outcome | Outcome | choice | [Repair; Replace; Credit; Scrap; Return as is]
rule rpe_rows.ru_confirmed | equals | Confirmed | #FDE7E9 | bold
section rpe_summary | Summary | 3
f rpe_total | Units evaluated | calc | {COUNTA(rpe_rows.ru_serial)}
f rpe_confirmed_count | Failures confirmed | calc | {COUNTIF(rpe_rows.ru_confirmed, "Confirmed")}
f rpe_nff | No fault found | calc | {COUNTIF(rpe_rows.ru_confirmed, "Not confirmed - no fault found")}
f rpe_capa | Corrective action | record
use customer_signatures
end

template customer-investigation | Customer Investigation | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags complaint investigation, root cause
purpose Investigate a customer complaint: contain, find the cause, decide the correction and corrective action, and assess whether other customers or products are affected.
scope Complaints that need investigation.
instructions Contain first, then investigate. Record whether other lots, products or customers are affected. Link a corrective action when the cause is systemic.
workflow Opened, contained, investigated, actions decided, response sent, closed.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use customer_header
section inv_containment | Containment | 2
f cvi_complaint | Complaint | record | *
f cvi_containment | Containment actions | longtext | *
f cvi_stock_checked | Stock and work in process checked | boolean
f cvi_other_customers | Other customers possibly affected | boolean
section inv_cause | Investigation | 2
f cvi_method | Method | multichoice | [Five whys; Fishbone; Is and is not; Data analysis; Failure analysis; Process review]
f cvi_occurrence | Cause of occurrence | longtext | *
f cvi_escape | Cause of escape | longtext
f cvi_confirmed | Cause confirmed | boolean
f cvi_capa | Corrective action | record
use action_plan, customer_signatures
end

template customer-response | Customer Response | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags customer response, complaint closure, letter
purpose Prepare the organization's formal response to a customer complaint: what was found, what was done and what will prevent recurrence.
scope Complaints that need a formal response.
instructions Answer in plain terms. State the containment, the cause and the actions with dates. Responses are approved before they are sent.
workflow Drafted, approved, sent, customer acceptance recorded.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use customer_header
section resp | Response | 1
f cr_complaint | Complaint | record | *
f cr_summary | Summary of the complaint | longtext | *
f cr_findings | What we found | longtext | *
f cr_containment | Containment | longtext | *
f cr_actions | Corrective actions and dates | longtext | *
f cr_due | Response due | date
f cr_sent | Sent on | date
f cr_on_time | Sent on time | calc | {IF(AND(ISNUMBER(DAYS(cr_sent, cr_due))), IF(DAYS(cr_sent, cr_due) <= 0, "Yes", "No"), "")}
f cr_customer_accepts | Customer accepted the response | choice | [Awaiting; Accepted; Not accepted]
rule cr_on_time | equals | No | #FFF4D6 | bold
use customer_signatures
end

template warranty-evaluation | Warranty Evaluation | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags warranty, claim evaluation
purpose Evaluate a warranty claim against the warranty terms and the evidence, decide acceptance and record the cost and any recovery.
scope Warranty claims from customers and dealers.
instructions Check coverage first (period, use and terms), then the failure. Record the cost. Supplier-caused failures are charged back where agreed.
workflow Claim received, coverage checked, failure evaluated, decision approved, settled.
retention Keep for the warranty period plus the retention period set by the organization.
use customer_header
section wty | Claim | 3
f we_claim | Claim number | text | *
f we_in_service | In service since | date
f we_failed_on | Failed on | date | *
f we_period_months | Warranty period (months) | integer | * min=0
f we_age_days | Age at failure (days) | calc | {DAYS(we_failed_on, we_in_service)}
f we_in_period | Within warranty period | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(we_age_days), IF(we_age_days <= we_period_months * 30.4, "Yes", "No"), "")}
f we_usage | Usage at failure | text
rule we_in_period | equals | No | #FFF4D6 | bold
section wty_decision | Decision | 3
f we_failure | Failure confirmed | choice | [Confirmed; Not confirmed; Not evaluated]
f we_cause | Cause | choice | [Manufacturing; Design; Supplier; Misuse; Wear; Unknown]
f we_decision | Decision | choice | * [Accepted; Accepted as goodwill; Rejected]
f we_parts_cost | Parts | currency | min=0
f we_labour_cost | Labour | currency | min=0
f we_other_cost | Other | currency | min=0
f we_total | Total cost | calc | {we_parts_cost + we_labour_cost + we_other_cost} dec=2
f we_recovery | Recoverable from supplier | currency | min=0
f we_net | Net cost | calc | {we_total - we_recovery} dec=2
use customer_signatures
end

template field-failure | Field Failure | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags field failure, reliability
purpose Record a failure of product in use: the conditions, the failure mode, the effect on the user and the analysis, and feed reliability and design data.
scope Failures in service reported by customers, service or monitoring.
instructions Record the operating conditions and hours or cycles. Assess the effect on safety. Trends across field failures are reviewed for recall assessment.
workflow Reported, analysed, actions decided, closed.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization.
use customer_header
section ff | Failure | 3
f ff_hours | Hours or cycles at failure | number | min=0
f ff_environment | Operating environment | text
f ff_mode | Failure mode | text | *
f ff_effect | Effect on the user | longtext | *
f ff_safety | Safety effect | boolean | *
f ff_injury | Injury or damage reported | boolean
f ff_analysis | Analysis | longtext
f ff_cause | Cause | text
f ff_recall_review | Recall assessment needed | calc | {IF(OR(ff_safety, ff_injury), "Yes", "No")}
rule ff_recall_review | equals | Yes | #FDE7E9 | bold
use customer_signatures
end

template recall-assessment | Recall Assessment | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags recall, field action, health hazard
purpose Assess whether a field problem needs a recall or field action: the hazard, the population affected, the likelihood and the decision, with the notifications required.
scope Problems with product in the field that may affect safety, compliance or performance.
instructions Define the affected population by lot, serial and date. Assess severity and probability. The decision and the notifications are approved by the people the organization authorizes.
workflow Opened, population defined, risk assessed, decision approved, notifications made.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the retention period set by the organization, or longer where regulation requires.
confidential
section ra_problem | Problem | 2
f rc_problem | Problem | longtext | *
f rc_source | Source records | record
f rc_product | Product | product | *
f rc_population | Affected population (lots, serials, dates) | longtext | *
f rc_units_shipped | Units shipped | integer | * min=0
f rc_units_field | Units estimated in use | integer | min=0
section ra_risk | Risk | 3
f rc_severity | Severity (1 to 5) | integer | * min=1 max=5
f rc_probability | Probability (1 to 5) | integer | * min=1 max=5
f rc_score | Risk score | calc | {rc_severity * rc_probability}
f rc_level | Risk level | calc | {IF(rc_score >= 15, "High", IF(rc_score >= 8, "Medium", "Low"))}
rule rc_level | equals | High | #FDE7E9 | bold
section ra_decision | Decision | 2
f rc_decision | Decision | choice | * [No action; Monitor; Field correction; Recall; Stop shipment]
f rc_rationale | Rationale | longtext | *
f rc_regulator | Regulator notification required | boolean
f rc_customers | Customer notification required | boolean
f rc_recall_record | Recall record | record
use customer_signatures
end

template csr-register | Customer-Specific Requirement Register | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags customer-specific requirements, CSR, register
purpose Register each customer's specific requirements, where each is addressed in the management system and who owns it, and track revisions.
scope Customers with specific requirements.
instructions List each requirement with its source document and revision. Record where it is addressed (procedure, form, plan). Review when the customer issues a new revision.
workflow Maintained, reviewed at each customer revision, approved.
retention Keep each revision for the retention period set by the organization.
landscape
section csrr | Register | 2
f csrg_customer | Customer | customer | *
f csrg_source | Source document and revision | text | *
f csrg_checked | Last checked for new revision | date
section csrr_rows | Requirements | 1
table csrg_rows | Requirements | 1
c cg_ref | Reference | text | *
c cg_summary | Requirement (own summary) | longtext | *
c cg_where | Addressed in | text | *
c cg_owner | Owner | user
c cg_status | Status | choice | * [Addressed; Partly addressed; Not addressed; Not applicable]
rule csrg_rows.cg_status | equals | Not addressed | #FDE7E9 | bold
f cg_open | Not addressed | calc | {COUNTIF(csrg_rows.cg_status, "Not addressed") + COUNTIF(csrg_rows.cg_status, "Partly addressed")}
use customer_signatures
end

template customer-satisfaction-review | Customer Satisfaction Review | CUSTOMER_QUALITY
tags customer satisfaction, perception, scorecards
purpose Review the customer's perception of performance from scorecards, surveys, complaints and delivery data, and decide improvement actions.
scope Customers reviewed at the frequency the organization sets.
instructions Enter each source with its result and the target. Results below target need an action.
workflow Compiled, reviewed, actions assigned, input to management review.
retention Keep for the retention period set by the organization.
section csr_scope | Scope | 3
f cs_customer | Customer | customer | *
f cs_period | Period | text | *
f cs_reviewer | Reviewer | user | *
section csr_sources | Sources | 1
table cs_rows | Measures | 1
c cs_source | Source | choice | * [Customer scorecard; Survey; Complaints; Delivery performance; Returns; Visits and meetings]
c cs_measure | Measure | text | *
c cs_result | Result | number | dec=2
c cs_target | Target | number | dec=2
c cs_higher_better | Higher is better | boolean
c cs_met | Target met | calc | {IF(AND(ISNUMBER(cs_result), ISNUMBER(cs_target)), IF(cs_higher_better, IF(cs_result >= cs_target, "Yes", "No"), IF(cs_result <= cs_target, "Yes", "No")), "")}
rule cs_rows.cs_met | equals | No | #FDE7E9 | bold
f cs_missed | Targets missed | calc | {COUNTIF(cs_rows.cs_met, "No")}
use action_plan, customer_signatures
end
